    <sectiondef kind="typedef">
      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group__posix__option__group__semaphores_1ga074f89c3e487ac90a9e7bea3c6a22bac" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>struct sys_sem</type>
        <definition>typedef struct sys_sem sem_t</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>sem_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Semaphore object type. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A <computeroutput>sem_t</computeroutput> may live in any memory the calling thread can access (static, stack, or heap). Sharing one between threads requires memory every participant can access: with <computeroutput>CONFIG_USERSPACE</computeroutput> enabled, a user thread&apos;s stack is private to it, so a shared <computeroutput>sem_t</computeroutput> belongs in static storage, a common memory partition, or the malloc arena. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
